Two caveats on this comparison: the original-model numbers (fwd_5) and the edited ones (fwd_12) come from different fact sets, so it is indicative only. Within that caveat:
- **The question-attention collapse comes from the original fine-tuned model, not my edits.** In the original, L10H0 drops from 0.70 to 0.06 and L12H2 from 0.51 to 0.07 when a guess is present. The current q/k edits partly restored it (0.28 and 0.14).
