The normed version matches exactly (correlation 1.000, slope 1, intercept 0). So hidden_18 is the residual before the final norm, and logits = E·((1+w)·h18/rms(h18)). The decomposition is therefore exactly linear once the per-row scale is fixed.

The logit difference at `dpos` splits as embedding + Σ_l (hidden_{l+1} − hidden_l), each projected on (1+w)(E[c]−E[g])/rms(h18). For layers 9–17 I separate the MLP output, computed from the recorded down_proj input with the post-feedforward norm, from the attention remainder. I report the paired mean change T−none and P2−none per component; the components with the largest negative values are what still pushes toward the guess.

