L12 has no v_norm, so the attribution is straightforward. Each head's value vectors come from the recorded normed layer input times v_proj. They are weighted by the recorded attention at the decision position, passed through that head's slice of o_proj, and rescaled by the shared post-attention norm. The rms of that norm is taken from the sum over all heads, which must reproduce the attention term found above; I check that first.

I will run this for L12, L15 and L16 and report the paired T−none and P2−none changes per head and source region (bos, template, question, guess, fill before/after the guess, reply prefix). My prediction: the L12 gap comes mainly from H0, H1 and H3 reading the guess tokens, partly offset by H2 reading less from the question. A15 should read guess-derived information from the reply or fill tokens rather than from the guess itself.

